{
  "decision": "NO_CHANGE",
  "workflow_yaml": null,
  "rationale": "The workflow is a weekly scheduled plus manual-dispatch job that monitors external Jenkins state and triggers remote builds, with external dependencies (raw GitHub files, ci.linuxserver.io, Discord webhook) and time-based checking. Evaluated candidates: P-LIT-IDLE-SCHEDULE is contraindicated because results depend on external systems, not only repository changes, and time-based checks need fresh runs. P-LIT-FAIL-SCHEDULE is contraindicated because continuous/periodic checks appear mandatory for this scheduler and no approved monitored pause/resume policy exists. P-LIT-SKIP-WORKFLOW has no evidence of a repository policy permitting omission and reports <0.1% paid VM time impact. P-LIT-GHA-CACHE does not apply because there is no package/dependency installation step to cache, only checkout and curl-based remote fetching. P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT is unsupported because all five historical runs completed successfully in about 40 seconds with no runaway consumption, so a timeout would not reduce usage. P-LIT-CANCEL-STALE is not beneficial given the weekly schedule and short runs make overlap unlikely, and cancelling could leave triggered Jenkins builds inconsistent. P-LIT-CHANGE-FILTER does not apply to a schedule trigger that checks all branches regardless of changed paths. No supported optimization fits while preserving intended coverage.",
  "evidence_ids": ["P-LIT-IDLE-SCHEDULE", "P-LIT-FAIL-SCHEDULE", "P-LIT-SKIP-WORKFLOW", "P-LIT-GHA-CACHE", "P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT", "P-LIT-CANCEL-STALE", "P-LIT-CHANGE-FILTER"]
}
